WEBVTT

00:00.900 --> 00:05.100
Your customers write from everywhere — email,
your website, Slack, Telegram.

00:05.150 --> 00:08.610
Spooldesk brings all of it into one
place, on a server you control.

00:08.660 --> 00:10.630
Let me show you how it works.

00:11.230 --> 00:12.700
This is the ticket queue.

00:12.750 --> 00:15.860
Every conversation lands here,
whatever channel it came from.

00:15.910 --> 00:20.760
Filter by team, category or operator — or just
search for what you remember.

00:21.960 --> 00:23.726
Open a ticket and you get the whole story:

00:23.776 --> 00:25.789
who's asking, what they wrote,
and where it came from.

00:26.430 --> 00:27.850
Type your reply right here.

00:27.900 --> 00:30.759
The moment you send it, the ticket
moves to waiting for the customer —

00:30.809 --> 00:31.948
nobody has to track that by hand.

00:33.580 --> 00:35.960
Need a colleague's help?
Leave an internal note.

00:36.010 --> 00:39.200
Your team sees it. The customer never does.

00:40.100 --> 00:44.160
The board shows the same work
by stage — new, in progress, waiting.

00:44.210 --> 00:46.850
One look, and you know what needs you next.

00:47.550 --> 00:49.910
The answers you give every
day become templates.

00:49.960 --> 00:53.730
One click, instead of typing the
same thing for the fortieth time.

00:54.430 --> 00:57.630
And when an answer deserves
to last, put it in the help centre.

00:57.680 --> 01:01.420
Customers find it on their own, and
every article has a link you can send.

01:02.120 --> 01:04.060
Channels are switched on in Integrations.

01:04.110 --> 01:05.904
Connect only what your team actually uses —

01:05.954 --> 01:08.188
each one comes with a checklist,
so you know it really works.

01:09.970 --> 01:11.790
Then there's the AI assistant.

01:11.840 --> 01:14.277
Ask it in plain words — which
tickets still need a reply? —

01:14.327 --> 01:15.551
and you get the answer in seconds.

01:16.080 --> 01:19.200
It can also suggest a change,
like moving a ticket forward.

01:19.250 --> 01:21.600
But nothing happens until you confirm.

01:22.300 --> 01:24.730
You can also let AI answer customers directly.

01:24.780 --> 01:28.260
Choose a single reply or a whole
conversation, and set the limits.

01:28.310 --> 01:32.590
It steps aside the moment a person takes
over, or the customer asks for one.

01:33.390 --> 01:36.218
Reports show how you're doing:
response times, resolution,

01:36.268 --> 01:38.047
customer satisfaction — by team
and by operator.

01:40.250 --> 01:43.580
Spooldesk runs on your own server,
so your data stays under your control.

01:43.630 --> 01:47.980
Try the live demo at spooldesk.net — and
when you're ready, install it yourself.
